@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Future after MVP. Provider, advanced Sprint/review, or untrusted execution requirement retained as deferred.
title AFTER MVP — Resumefolio | Git review and merge
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #64748B
skinparam activity {
 BackgroundColor #DBEAFE
 BorderColor #64748B
 FontColor #17324D
 DiamondBackgroundColor #FEF3C7
 DiamondBorderColor #B45309
 StartColor #17324D
 EndColor #17324D
}
start
:Identify pull request, source / target and current revisions;
if (Actor has required merge authority?) then (yes)
 :Evaluate current request, review and target policies;
 if (Current conditions eligible?) then (yes)
  :Evaluate merge with selected strategy and current target;
  if (Allowed result without unresolved conflict?) then (yes)
   :Apply only the eligible merge under defined concurrent-update rules;
   if (Completion established?) then (yes)
    :Record resulting history and actual merged outcome; <<#DCFCE7>>
   else (failed / uncertain)
    :Record bounded outcome and reconciliation needs; <<#FEF3C7>>
   endif
  else (conflict / changed state)
   :Retain unmerged outcome and show permitted resolution path; <<#FEF3C7>>
  endif
 else (no)
  :Report unmet conditions without false merged status; <<#FEF3C7>>
 endif
else (no)
 :Deny merge without protected disclosure; <<#FEF3C7>>
endif
stop
legend bottom
Conceptual flow; no merge strategy or approval count selected.
Updated revisions require defined review / conflict handling.
A merge does not inherently authorize production deployment.
endlegend
